<title>GERMANY: German car output halted by Spanish trucker strike.</title>
<headline>German car output halted by Spanish trucker strike.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>German carmakers Volkswagen AG and Adam Opel AG, a unit of General Motors Corp, said on Monday they would have to suspend some vehicle production due to the ongoing trucker strike in Spain.</p>
<p>VW said it would halt production of its Polo subcompact vehicle as of Tuesday due to parts shortages.</p>
<p>Opel said it would halt production of its Astra subcompact vehicle as of Wednesday. The carmaker said its component factory in Kaiserslautern would be affected by the strike.</p>
<p>Opel has already interrupted production of its popular Vectra saloon at its plant in Ruesselsheim, saying output of about 4,500 vehicles per week would be affected.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
